 "genre_note": "136 notes across 16 sub-plans. Distribution is what the enum predicts for news: ~85% empirical_observation, then concept (9 notes: MLB offseason market state, DFS contest scoring formats, CFP/NY6 structure, bowl betting market types). Rarer blocks appear only where the text genuinely supplies them and were not manufactured anywhere else: argument x7 (Heyman's conditional reasoning about Toronto trading Bichette/Guerrero; the Bills-Chargers pick with its grounds; futures-bet timing risk/reward; Liew on Ten Hag's attacking trade-off; Ronay on United's squad and decline; the Nations League prestige/congested-cycle case), counter_argument x2 (doc_0184 [4] explicitly rebuts the charge that Scotland under-tried \u2014 \"that would be unfair\" \u2014 and doc_0206 [6-10] rebuts the euphoria of the Toone win), model x2 (McTominay's role mechanism, Ronay's \"three concurrent roles\" framework for a United manager), procedure x2 (the weekly DFS sleeper method, opening a sportsbook account). hypothesis: ZERO instances. Nothing in 20 sports documents states a testable prediction as a hypothesis rather than as a reported claim or an argued judgement; the closest candidate (Blue Jays trading infielders if they sign Ohtani) is a claim with stated grounds, so it is filed as argument. Absence recorded rather than filled. navigation: none produced, per instruction. Cross-document entity sharing: Ohtani (doc_0422+doc_0426), the WI-England T20 series outcome / Shai Hope / Adil Rashid / England's 132 all out / the England camp verdict (doc_0063+doc_0064+doc_0371), SuperDraft and DraftKings/FanDuel scoring formats (doc_0386+doc_0583+doc_0544 \u2014 verbatim-repeated boilerplate that would otherwise have been three near-duplicate notes), Ten Hag's blame/pressure (doc_0242+doc_0370), and England's defensive brittleness (doc_0184+doc_0206). Splitting discipline: doc_0150 is a 12-game roundup and doc_0093 a 6-match roundup \u2014 each was split per match rather than merged, since a merged roundup note would be retrieved for everything and answer nothing; doc_0422 (3,475 words, ~60 tracker entries) was split by transaction subject, not by word count, which is why Yamamoto's meetings tour is one 700-word note while Matt Carpenter's release is a 70-word note. Coverage: 15 of 20 documents land at 92-98% of words assigned. Five land lower and all five are chrome-heavy Guardian pages, not compression failures \u2014 doc_0093 ~83% and doc_0371 ~81% (each carries the identical 84-word \"how to sign up for sport breaking news alerts\" app guide plus a ~90-word newsletter-promotion block), doc_0206 ~88%, doc_0184 ~90%, doc_0242 ~89% and doc_0370 ~90% (each one 89-102-word newsletter promotion). Nothing dropped states a scope condition on its document's central claim: I re-read every dropped block, and the only borderline calls were doc_0449 [4] (\"Chad Ryland redeems himself with game-winning field goal\") and doc_0447 [5]/[11], all of which are read-more links whose substance is fully carried by assigned blocks in the same document. The \"Updated at HH.MM GMT\" timestamps in the two cricket live blogs (20 blocks, 4 words each) are the only other systematic drop."
